        "app_name": "Response Stimulation Experiment - ContentsDa Science Experiment",
        "release_date": "1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "description": "1. Watch and catch the ruler falling in a well-lit area.\n2. Listen to the sound of the ruler falling in the dark and catch it.\n\n<Result\n1. when looking and catching: light stimulus → visual cell → visual nerve → cerebrum → spinal cord → motor nerve → hand muscle → reaction (catching the ruler)\n2 When listening and grasping: sound stimulus → auditory cells → auditory nerve → cerebrum → spinal cord → motor nerve → hand muscles → response (grasping the ruler)\n\n Understand that this is due to the different pathways the stimulus travels and the different speeds at which the brain processes information about the stimulus",
